{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally on the Aegean Sea"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Dead Sea"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Out and About in the City > Istanbul"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the comparative form to compare two things."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's is saltier than most lakes. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The comparative form ends in -er: <span class=\"italic\">taller</span>. <br>The word more is used with longer words: <span class=\"italic\">more beautiful</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the comparative with a noun: <span class=\"italic\">a bigger car, his car was older.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the comparative with than: <span class=\"italic\">his house is larger than my house, this dress is more expensive than that one.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The water is denser. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Functional Language "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you ask where things are, you use polite questions.<br><br>  When you say where things are you often use prepositions of place.  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking Where Things Are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Saying Where Things Are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me ... ?<br> I'd like to know ... <br>Do you know where ... ?<br> Where is ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is between ... <br> They are below ... <br>He is in ... <br>They are at ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It lies <span class=\"strong\">between </span> Israel and Jordan. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is about 1,300 feet <span class=\"strong\">below </span> sea level. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He went swimming <span class=\"strong\">in</span> the Dead Sea."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lowest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "closest to the ground, near the bottom  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The Dead Sea is the lowest spot on earth."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the Dead Sea."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le05ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " below "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " lower than or under something else  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We found shells just below the surface of the water."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "salty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to taste or smell like salt  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Dead Sea is very salty."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dense"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "thick; heavy  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Dead Sea water is dense as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to float"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stay on the surface of the water  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People can float on the surface of the Dead Sea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sea "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large area of salt water "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The ship travelled by sea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "baths"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " hot water with minerals for soaking in  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I tried all the different baths at the spa."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "luxurious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very comfortable and expensive lifestyle  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The spa was very luxurious."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look on the internet and research a body of water."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 6 - 8 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe where the water is and the land surrounding it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say who goes there and when."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write 50 - 75 words about a body of water in my country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use describing words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my sentences to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le05ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le05ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Sally's Suitcase<br><br>The Dead Sea is the lowest spot on the earth. Where is it? It lies between Israel and Jordan. It is about 1,300 feet below sea level. It's saltier than most lakes, and the water is denser. Even people who can't swim can float! There are no fish or plants here. That is why they call it the Dead Sea.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "I'm staying in a beautiful hotel. It's a health spa with special baths. The spas here are larger and more luxurious than at home! People come here to feel better and get healthier. They stay for a week or even longer!", "id": 2, "time": "26800", "image": "engenn5le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Today I went swimming in the Dead Sea. It was amazing. The water was very warm and it felt like oil. You would love it!", "id": 3, "time": "42500", "image": "engenn5le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Vocabulary and Grammar"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about geographic features. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say where places are in a country.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can compare two things."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you prefer to swim in salty ocean water or a pool? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you like best about swimming?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {